  "text": "Mary Magdalene was the first to preach the resurrection. John chapter twenty. She comes to the tomb while it is still dark, sees the stone taken away, and runs to Peter and John. They race back, look inside, see the linen clothes, and then the text says they went away again unto their own home. She does not. Mary stood without at the sepulchre weeping. Everyone else left. She stayed and cried in a graveyard. So she is the one who is there when two angels ask why she is weeping, and she is the one who turns around and sees him standing there, and supposes him to be the gardener. Sir, she says, if thou have borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away. She is grieving and she is still trying to do the practical thing. And he says one word. Mary. And she knows. Then he sends her. Go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father. And Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples that she had seen the Lord. The whole faith starts with a woman running with news.",
